From: Mark Chiou <chiouss@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: qca808x: only bypass blink check without speed/duplex rules

qca808x_led_parse_netdev() always sets BLINK_CHECK_BYPASS, which makes
the LED follow the TX/RX blink trigger even when the speed or duplex
condition of the rule doesn't match. This is needed for rules with only
tx and/or rx, but for a rule like "link_2500 tx rx" the LED is off at a
1000Mbps link and still blinks on traffic.

Only set BLINK_CHECK_BYPASS when the rule has no speed or duplex
condition, so that a LED only blinks on traffic while it is lit for
the configured link speed or duplex.

Signed-off-by: Mark Chiou <chiouss@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca808x.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca808x.c
@@ -445,10 +445,18 @@
 	if (rules && !*offload_trigger)
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 
-	/* Enable BLINK_CHECK_BYPASS by default to make the LED
-	 * blink even with duplex or speed mode not enabled.
+	/* Enable BLINK_CHECK_BYPASS to make the LED blink even with duplex
+	 * or speed mode not enabled. When a speed or duplex mode is enabled,
+	 * only blink while that condition matches, so that e.g. a LED for
+	 * link_2500 doesn't blink on traffic at 1000Mbps.
 	 */
-	*offload_trigger |= QCA808X_LED_BLINK_CHECK_BYPASS;
+	if (!(*offload_trigger & (QCA808X_LED_SPEED10_ON |
+				  QCA808X_LED_SPEED100_ON |
+				  QCA808X_LED_SPEED1000_ON |
+				  QCA808X_LED_SPEED2500_ON |
+				  QCA808X_LED_HALF_DUPLEX_ON |
+				  QCA808X_LED_FULL_DUPLEX_ON)))
+		*offload_trigger |= QCA808X_LED_BLINK_CHECK_BYPASS;
 
 	return 0;
 }
